From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:01:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Confirm threaded SQLite close before preparing a replacement

Reserve the storage identity before the WAL scan and carry that reservation through the SQLite connection. On synchronous close, enqueue the existing CLOSED record and then release the reservation. A replacement tree waits for every connection of the previous tree, including retained facets. An unconfirmed close keeps the reservation until this child generation exits.

Cover retained connections, the CLOSED and OPEN wire order, an unrelated identity, canceled preparation, and a BUSY SQLite close with a controlled WAL peer.

